{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1f0c0de-0000-4000-8000-quickecommerce1",
    "name": "quick-ecommerce (MaLLADE) — Backend API",
    "description": "Full backend API surface for the MaLLADE storefront, reachable through the TLS gateway on :8443.\n\n## How to use\n1. Import this collection AND `quick-ecommerce.postman_environment.json` (the matching environment), then select that environment top-right.\n2. Set `baseUrl` (default `https://localhost:8443`; for prod use `https://mallde.in`).\n3. Postman will hit a self-signed cert on localhost — turn OFF SSL verification (Settings → General → SSL certificate verification) for local. mallde.in has a real Cloudflare cert.\n4. Mint a token first:\n   - **Auth → Guest token** → saves `guestToken` (browse + cart, NOT checkout).\n   - **Auth → Register** or **Auth → Login** → saves `userToken` (real account; needed for checkout/orders).\n   - **Auth → Login (as ADMIN)** → saves `adminToken` (admin endpoints). Use your admin@mallade.test credentials.\n   These use test scripts that auto-capture the returned `token` into collection variables — no copy/paste.\n5. Auth'd requests reference `{{userToken}}` / `{{adminToken}}` / `{{guestToken}}` via Bearer auth automatically.\n\n## Gotchas baked into the requests\n- Login/Register field is `identifier` (email OR phone), NOT `email`.\n- Honey SKUs 400 at POST /api/cart/items (\"coming soon\") — use a `category:fruit` productId.\n- Checkout requires a NON-guest JWT (guest-* tokens 403) AND an `Idempotency-Key` header (missing = 400).\n- Oversell guard is two-layer: Redis ATP fast-check (409) + DB pessimistic lock (durable).\n- Admin endpoints are doubly gated (gateway RBAC + in-service AdminRoleFilter).\n- order-service `/admin/orders/**` are NOT gateway-routed (admin-app internal only) — documented but unreachable via baseUrl.\n- Internal saga endpoints (inventory reservations/commit/release, payments charge, co-purchase) are service-to-service; included for testing/debug, not normal client flows.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "https://localhost:8443" },
    { "key": "guestToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "productId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "sku", "value": "FRT-001" },
    { "key": "orderId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "callGrant", "value": "" },
    { "key": "topic", "value": "honey" },
    { "key": "otpPhone", "value": "+919999999999" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Guest token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().token;",
                  "if (t) { pm.collectionVariables.set('guestToken', t); console.log('saved guestToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Guest\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/guest", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "guest"] },
            "description": "Public. Mints a short-lived GUEST JWT (browse + cart, but checkout 403s on guest-* tokens). `name` is required (1-40 chars)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().token;",
                  "if (t) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', t); console.log('saved userToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"buyer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Test Buyer\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
            "description": "Public self-serve signup. `identifier` = email OR phone (max 120, validated), `password` 8-72 chars, `displayName` optional. 400 if identifier format invalid."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().token;",
                  "if (t) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', t); console.log('saved userToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"buyer@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password123\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Public. Field is `identifier` (email OR phone), NOT `email`. Generic 401 on any mismatch (anti-enumeration). Saves userToken."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (as ADMIN)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().token;",
                  "if (t) { pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', t); console.log('saved adminToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"identifier\": \"admin@mallade.test\",\n  \"password\": \"CHANGE_ME_ADMIN_PASSWORD\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Same /auth/login endpoint — log in as your ADMIN user (role=ADMIN) and this saves the JWT to `adminToken` for the admin folders. Use the password stamped onto admin@mallade.test (the authdb BCrypt password, NOT nginx basic-auth)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "OTP — request",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{otpPhone}}\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/request", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "request"] },
            "description": "Public. Always returns {sent:true} regardless of phone validity (no enumeration oracle). `devCode` only echoed when OTP_DEV_ECHO=true. phone pattern ^\\+?[0-9]{8,15}$."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "OTP — verify",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (j && j.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', j.token); console.log('saved userToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{otpPhone}}\",\n  \"code\": \"123456\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"] },
            "description": "Public. code = 4-8 digits. 429 if too many attempts; generic 401 on mismatch. On success saves userToken."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Google Sign-In",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"credential\": \"GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN_HERE\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "auth", "google"] },
            "description": "Public. Exchanges a Google ID-token for a JWT (Taste Match V7). Returns clean 503 {disabled:true} when GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is not configured. credential max 4096 chars."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{userToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Requires Bearer JWT. Returns the current account's profile. Gateway injects X-User-Id from the token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update display name",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (j && j.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('userToken', j.token); console.log('refreshed userToken'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{userToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"displayName\": \"New Name\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me/display-name", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me", "display-name"] },
            "description": "Requires Bearer JWT. displayName 1-40 chars. Returns a fresh JWT (re-saved to userToken)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Catalog — Browse & Search",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products?size=200&page=0",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "catalog", "products"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "size", "value": "200", "description": "default 20; use 200 so newest SKUs aren't paged off (smoke gotcha)" },
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "category", "value": "fruit", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "type", "value": "FRUIT", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. Paginated product list. Default page size = 20 — pass ?size=200 to see everything."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get product by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/{{productId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "catalog", "products", "{{productId}}"] },
            "description": "Public. Single product detail. 404 if missing."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Search products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/search?q=litchi&size=20&page=0",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "catalog", "products", "search"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "q", "value": "litchi" },
                { "key": "size", "value": "20" },
                { "key": "page", "value": "0" },
                { "key": "category", "value": "fruit", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "type", "value": "FRUIT", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public. OpenSearch-backed. Blank q returns normal browse; degrades to ILIKE when search is unavailable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Recommendations for product",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/products/{{productId}}/recommendations?size=8",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "catalog", "products", "{{productId}}", "recommendations"],
              "query": [{ "key": "size", "value": "8" }]
            },
            "description": "Public. Hybrid co-purchase + content-based. Best-effort (returns [] never 503); 404 only if anchor product missing."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Catalog — Notify (launch interest)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Notify signup",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"topic\": \"honey\",\n  \"name\": \"Test User\",\n  \"source\": \"postman\",\n  \"fruits\": [\"litchi\", \"mango\"],\n  \"phone\": \"9999999999\",\n  \"email\": \"buyer@example.com\",\n  \"pincode\": \"560001\",\n  \"city\": \"Bangalore\",\n  \"state\": \"Karnataka\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/notify", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "catalog", "notify"] },
            "description": "Public. Launch-interest signup (honey teaser / fruit quiz / fruit-xi demand). REQUIRED: topic, phone (10-digit Indian mobile), pincode (6-digit), city, state. Idempotent on (topic, phone). fruits = per-fruit demand fan-out. WARNING: this writes a real demand row — do NOT spam against prod."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Notify count",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/notify/count?topic={{topic}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "catalog", "notify", "count"],
              "query": [{ "key": "topic", "value": "{{topic}}" }]
            },
            "description": "Public. Aggregate count only (no PII). topic required."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Catalog — Fruit XI (WC-2026)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Teams",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/fruit-xi/teams", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "catalog", "fruit-xi", "teams"] },
            "description": "Public. Static WC-2026 team roster (code, name, flag, kit colours)."
          }
        },
